== Part 1: F, U, S at p^2, pq, p^2 q (trial division, all primes < 400) ==
  p^2  : (F, U, S) = (1, 1, 1),  F - U - S = -1;  confirmed on 78 prime choices
  pq   : (F, U, S) = (2, 2, 2),  F - U - S = -2;  confirmed on 6006 prime choices
  p^2q : (F, U, S) = (4, 2, 3),  F - U - S = -1;  confirmed on 6006 prime choices
  slow independent trial-division path agrees on 561 cases (primes < 60)
  controls (balanced shapes):
    p = 7              (F,U,S) = (0,0,0)  balanced
    p^3 = 27           (F,U,S) = (2,1,1)  balanced
    p^3 = 8            (F,U,S) = (2,1,1)  balanced
    p^2qr = 60         (F,U,S) = (10,3,7)  balanced
    p^2qr = 2^2*7*11   (F,U,S) = (10,3,7)  balanced
  hostiles:
    q = p in pq -> p^2 (p=5)             (F,U,S) = (1,1,1), defect -1
    q = p in p^2q -> p^3 (p=5)           (F,U,S) = (2,1,1), defect +0
    literal p^q r, p=2,q=3,r=5 -> 2^3*5  (F,U,S) = (6,2,3), defect +1
    pqr = 30                             (F,U,S) = (6,3,6), defect -3
  (the collision q = p sends p^2 q to the balanced shape p^3: the defect jumps -1 -> 0)

== Part 2: exhaustive defect level sets for 2 <= N <= 2000000 ==
  defect -7: profiles(count) (1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1):48
  defect -6: profiles(count) (1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1):3465
