  defect -2: profiles(count) (1, 1):407061
  defect -1: profiles(count) (2,):223, (2, 1):82145
  defect +0: profiles(count) (1,):148933, (2, 1, 1):170462, (3,):30
  verdict: delta = -1 exactly at p^2 and p^2 q; delta = -2 exactly at pq;
           delta = 0 exactly at p, p^3, p^2 q r; every other delta < 0 is a squarefree
           composite with delta = -omega (DB2 of arithmetic_braids, re-run exhaustively).

== Part 3: prime-adjunction recursion delta(N r) = 2 delta(N) + U(N) - [N sqfree] - [N prime] ==
  recursion verified on 59997 pairs (N <= 20000, three primes r per N)
  chains:  p  --(x q)-->  pq        :  0  -> -2   (away from balance)
           p^2 --(x q)--> p^2 q     : -1  -> -1   (2(-1) + U(p^2) = -2 + 1)
           p^2 q --(x r)--> p^2 q r : -1  ->  0   (2(-1) + U(p^2 q) = -2 + 2)
           p^2 --(x p)--> p^3       : -1  ->  0   (exponent raise: tau 3 -> 4)

== Part 4: Klein orbits on D(p^2 q r) and the quadrant representatives ==
  orbit ['p^2q', 'p^2r', 'q', 'r']  ->  quadrant representative p^2q
  orbit ['p^2', 'qr']  ->  quadrant representative p^2
  orbit ['p', 'pqr']  ->  quadrant representative p
  orbit ['pq', 'pr']  ->  quadrant representative pq
  the four Klein orbits have quadrant representatives {p, p^2, pq, p^2 q} = p * Div(pq):
  the three asked shapes plus p, i.e. exactly the divisors of p^2 q divisible by p.

